WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
Choose a few criteria that describe the quality of the learning.

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:09.772
For our explanation, use evidence accuracy, reasoning and communication or access.

3
00:00:09.972 --> 00:00:13.300
RubricSplat can help organize the descriptors.

4
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.194
Keep them observable.

5
00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:22.904
A criterion such as uses two accurate observations is easier to act on than a vague label such as excellent effort.

6
00:00:23.104 --> 00:00:26.986
Good feedback can identify a strength and a next action.

7
00:00:27.186 --> 00:00:33.830
Say: your claim names a location; add the two temperature values and explain why they support it.

8
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.339
The learner can act on that message.

9
00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:41.986
Praise alone may feel encouraging but does not specify how to improve the explanation.

10
00:00:42.186 --> 00:00:49.264
Toneshifter or Vibe Check may support revision of a message, but the teacher must verify the meaning and respectful

11
00:00:49.464 --> 00:00:50.301
tone.

12
00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:55.032
Feedback is incomplete as a classroom routine if students never use it.

13
00:00:55.232 --> 00:01:01.947
Reserve time for a revision, ask learners to highlight the changed reasoning and check whether the action improved

14
00:01:02.147 --> 00:01:03.046
the work.

15
00:01:03.246 --> 00:01:09.397
The research figure for high-information feedback is a subgroup estimate, not a promise about this app.

16
00:01:09.597 --> 00:01:16.306
Pause and turn one vague comment into a criterion-based action, then revise the sample answer yourself.
